💡 How the USB Driver Hotplug Workflow Works
​USB Driver Injection: If you plug in a USB flash drive containing .deb driver files (e.g., custom Realtek or Broadcom driver packages), the background service automatically detects them.
​Auto-Installation: The system runs dpkg -i on the .deb files from the USB drive without needing command-line intervention.
​Local Caching: The installed .deb packages are cached locally in /var/cache/berry-router/drivers/ so they remain available even if the USB drive is removed.

